  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s SHAF2 drawing of a pattern in Shafai’s book: the design of Bourgoin’s plate 149 on a smaller square tile, a sixteen-pointed star at its centre and eight-pointed stars on its sides, every star split into kites. Every edge runs at a multiple of 11.25°. The star is the same, so the first four steps are shared. The tile’s half-side comes exactly from two corners of the star’s own lines, and every other line runs through a crossing of earlier lines. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. Wichmann colours each piece and its mirror image differently; we colour by shape. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data200/SHAF2: Shafai, page 248",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data200/SHAF2.html",
      "note": "Read from his finished drawing, not construction instructions. His reference is Javad Shafai, On decoration in Persian architecture and wood carving (Tehran, 1977), page 248, whose caption gives no place."
    }
